From: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Mar 2026 17:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: L3MH activate ES VTEP on Type-4 ESR

In L3-only EVPN Multi-Homing (no L2 VNI), remote VTEPs discovered via
Type-4 ES routes are never activated because evi_cnt remains 0 — there
are no EVI bindings without an L2 VNI.

Accept BGP_EVPNES_VTEP_ESR (set when a Type-4 ESR route is received)
as sufficient for VTEP activation, in addition to the existing evi_cnt
check.  This allows the remote ES VTEP to be sent to zebra for nexthop
group programming even in L3-only deployments.

Signed-off-by: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
---
 bgpd/bgp_evpn_mh.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bgpd/bgp_evpn_mh.c b/bgpd/bgp_evpn_mh.c
index abcdef123..456789abc 100644
--- a/bgpd/bgp_evpn_mh.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgp_evpn_mh.c
@@ -1445,7 +1445,8 @@ static enum zclient_send_status bgp_evpn_es_vtep_re_eval_active(
 	/* currently we need an active EVI reference to use the VTEP as
 	 * a nexthop. this may change...
 	 */
-	if (es_vtep->evi_cnt)
+	if (es_vtep->evi_cnt ||
+	    CHECK_FLAG(es_vtep->flags, BGP_EVPNES_VTEP_ESR))
 		SET_FLAG(es_vtep->flags, BGP_EVPNES_VTEP_ACTIVE);
 	else
 		UNSET_FLAG(es_vtep->flags, BGP_EVPNES_VTEP_ACTIVE);
